workedExamples.solution_text:
The line meets the axes at $(0,8)$ and $(4,0)$. The region is a triangle above the axis, with base $4$ and height $8$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=0.4cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{regionFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[regionFill] (0,0)--(0,8)--(4,0)--cycle;
\draw[black,->] (-0.5,0)--(5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-1)--(0,10) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (0,8)--(4,0);
\node[left] at (0,8) {$8$};
\node[below] at (4,0) {$4$};
\node[right] at (2,4) {$y=8-2x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\int_{0}^{4}(8-2x)\,dx\\&=\frac12(4)(8)\\&=16\end{aligned}$

The parallel sides have lengths $f(-1)=3$ and $f(2)=9$. Their perpendicular separation is $2-(-1)=3$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.4cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{regionFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[regionFill] (-1,0)--(-1,3)--(2,9)--(2,0)--cycle;
\draw[black,->] (-2,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-1)--(0,11) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (-1.5,2)--(2.5,10);
\draw[black] (-1,0)--(-1,3) (2,0)--(2,9);
\node[below] at (-1,0) {$-1$};
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[left] at (-1,3) {$(-1,3)$};
\node[right] at (2,9) {$(2,9)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The region lies above the axis.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\int_{-1}^{2}(2x+5)\,dx\\&=\frac32(3+9)\\&=18\end{aligned}$

The graph is the upper half of $x^{2}+y^{2}=36$, a circle of radius $6$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.35cm,y=0.35cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{regionFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[regionFill] (6,0) arc (0:180:6)--cycle;
\draw[black,->] (-7,0)--(8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-1)--(0,8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (6,0) arc (0:180:6);
\node[below] at (-6,0) {$-6$};
\node[below] at (6,0) {$6$};
\node[above left] at (0,6) {$6$};
\node[anchor=west] at (-7,9) {(a)};
\begin{scope}[xshift=7cm]
\fill[regionFill] (0,0)--(-6,0) arc (180:90:6)--cycle;
\draw[black,->] (-7,0)--(8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-1)--(0,8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (6,0) arc (0:180:6);
\node[below] at (-6,0) {$-6$};
\node[below right] at (0,0) {$0$};
\node[below] at (6,0) {$6$};
\node[above left] at (0,6) {$6$};
\node[anchor=west] at (-7,9) {(b)};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) The region is a semicircle.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\int_{-6}^{6}\sqrt{36-x^{2}}\,dx\\&=\frac12\pi(6)^2\\&=18\pi\end{aligned}$
(b) The region is a quarter circle.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\int_{-6}^{0}\sqrt{36-x^{2}}\,dx\\&=\frac14\pi(6)^2\\&=9\pi\end{aligned}$

The line crosses the axis at $x=2$. The triangle below the axis has base $2$ and height $4$; the triangle above has base $3$ and height $6$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.7cm,y=0.4cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{regionFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[regionFill] (0,0)--(0,-4)--(2,0)--cycle;
\fill[regionFill] (2,0)--(5,6)--(5,0)--cycle;
\draw[black,->] (-1,0)--(6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-5)--(0,8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (0,-4)--(5,6);
\draw[black] (5,0)--(5,6);
\node[left] at (0,-4) {$-4$};
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$5$};
\node[right] at (5,6) {$(5,6)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Count the area below the axis as negative.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\int_{0}^{5}(2x-4)\,dx\\&=-\frac12(2)(4)+\frac12(3)(6)\\&=-4+9\\&=5\end{aligned}$
(b) Count both areas as positive.
$\begin{aligned}A&=4+9\\&=13\text{ square units}\end{aligned}$

Split at $x=0$. Both triangles lie above the axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.5cm,y=0.5cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{regionFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[regionFill] (-3,0)--(-3,3)--(0,0)--(5,5)--(5,0)--cycle;
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-1)--(0,6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (-3,3)--(0,0)--(5,5);
\draw[black] (-3,0)--(-3,3) (5,0)--(5,5);
\node[below] at (-3,0) {$-3$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$5$};
\node[left] at (-3,3) {$(-3,3)$};
\node[right] at (5,5) {$(5,5)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}\int_{-3}^{5}|x|\,dx\\&=\frac12(3)(3)+\frac12(5)(5)\\&=\frac92+\frac{25}{2}\\&=17\end{aligned}$

