workedExamples.solution_text:
The parallel sides have lengths $4$ and $2k$, separated by $k-2$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.7cm,y=0.35cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{regionFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[regionFill] (2,0)--(2,4)--(5,10)--(5,0)--cycle;
\draw[black,->] (-0.5,0)--(6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-1)--(0,12) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(5.5,11);
\draw[black] (2,0)--(2,4) (5,0)--(5,10);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$k$};
\node[left] at (2,4) {$4$};
\node[right] at (5,10) {$2k$};
\node[right] at (3,6) {$y=2x$};
\node[below] at (3,-2) {Not to scale};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}32&=\frac{k-2}{2}(4+2k)\\32&=(k-2)(k+2)\\32&=k^2-4\\k^2&=36\\k&=6\end{aligned}$
Choose the positive root because $k>2$.

